# MAP.md — <project name>

> **Codebase map.** One-screen orientation for any agent or human landing
> in this repo cold. Lists top-level folders with one-line descriptions
> and owner teams. Linked from root `CLAUDE.md` as the first stop after
> session-start context.
>
> Keep it scannable — if it scrolls more than two screens, the repo is
> probably ready for module-level `MAP.md` files (one per top-level
> directory), not a longer root file.
>
> Source: Anthropic, ["How Claude Code Works in Large Codebases"](https://claude.com/blog/how-claude-code-works-in-large-codebases-best-practices-and-where-to-start) — *"Build codebase maps for unconventional structures."*

